invariant: INV-48
file: mlkem_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the row sampler stops after three blocks, so an entry whose stream
  needs a fourth keeps coefficients it never wrote, about one entry
  in a hundred, which bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test's cases are sure to
  hold. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    for (size_t read = 0; read < MLK_SAMPLE_GROUPS && !mlk_row_sampled(count);
--- new
    for (size_t read = 0; read < 3 * MLK_BLOCK_GROUPS && !mlk_row_sampled(count);
